## Why This Is Asked
 Tests ability to design a scalable, multi-tenant privacy enforcement and incident response workflow on GCP, including data lineage, per-tenant isolation, and automated remediation under real-time load.

## Key Concepts
 - Real-time data processing, per-tenant isolation, data masking, DLP, Vertex AI, Dataflow, Pub/Sub, Data Catalog lineage
 - Event-time vs processing-time semantics, idempotency, backpressure, rollback strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
function maskPII(record){
  const r = { ...record };
  if (r.ssn) r.ssn = '***-**-****';
  if (r.email) r.email = r.email.replace(/(.{1})(.*)(@)/, '$1***$2$3');
  return r;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the anomaly model under bursty traffic and schema drift?
- How would you handle false positives/negatives and post-incident cleanup?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design multi-tenant privacy-conscious streaming pipelines at scale using Pub/Sub, Dataflow, BigQuery, Vertex AI Feature Store, and Data Catalog. Emphasizes isolation, rollback, testing, fault tolerance, and latency vs. cost trade-offs.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant isolation with dedicated datasets and IAM
- Real-time scoring using Dataflow + Vertex AI Feature Store
- Privacy controls and data contracts via Data Catalog
- Rollback strategy (24h per tenant) and automated tests
- Regional failover and latency targets (sub-1s scoring, 5–10s ETL)

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-configuration snippet for multi-tenant pipeline
const config = {
  tenants: 'per-tenant',
  pipelines: {
    pubsubTopic: 'tenant-*-events',
    dataflow: {
      enrich: true,
      writes: {
        dataset: 'tenant_dataset',
        tablePartition: 'YYYYMM'
      }
    },
    scoring: {
      featureStore: 'tenant_fs',
      publish: 'tenant-scores'
    }
  },
  contracts: {
    catalog: 'tenant_contracts'
  },
  ops: {
    rollbackWindowHours: 24
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate latency under peak load and implement circuit breakers?
- What tests and tooling would verify the 24h rollback per tenant in production?

## Why This Is Asked

This question probes practical data quality, governance, rollback, and per-tenant isolation on GCP, with real components like Pub/Sub, Dataflow, BigQuery, Cloud Storage, Data Catalog, and time-travel. It also tests how to surface quality signals to dashboards and maintain lineage.

## Key Concepts

- Data quality framework per tenant (schema conformance, null checks, dedupe)
- Per-tenant isolation in BigQuery
- Data Catalog lineage and contract testing
- Rollback using BigQuery time travel and snapshots
- Testing strategy and drift monitoring

## Code Example

```javascript
// Sample validation stub for a record
function validate(rec){
  if(!rec.tenant_id) throw new Error("missing tenant_id");
  if(rec.event_time == null) return false;
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you implement per-tenant rollback with time travel and ensure consistency across dashboards?
- How would you scale the quality checks as tenants grow from 4 to 100+?

